(5201253, 756283, 97893, '<td valign="top">Very good that you spotted this.<br/> <br/>I did not know the meaning of the work, and I searched  Wiki<br/> <br/><i> <br/>"The Panopticon is a type of prison building designed by English philosopher and social theorist Jeremy Bentham in 1785. The concept of the design is to allow an observer to observe (-opticon) all (pan-) prisoners without the prisoners being able to tell whether they are being watched, thereby conveying what one architect has called the "sentiment of an invisible omniscience."[1]</i> <br/> <br/> <br/>Hey the cameras here are too obvious! :-))).</td>', 'Very good that you spotted this. I did not know the meaning of the work, and I searched  Wiki  "The Panopticon is a type of prison building designed by English philosopher and social theorist Jeremy Bentham in 1785. The concept of the design is to allow an observer to observe (-opticon) all (pan-) prisoners without the prisoners being able to tell whether they are being watched, thereby conveying what one architect has called the "sentiment of an invisible omniscience."[1]   Hey the cameras here are too obvious! :-))).', '2009-01-18 09:56:20.000000', NULL, 1),
