(5204359, 756086, 63218, '<td valign="top">First saw this on the Dell monitor at work &amp; thought "snapshot."  On the Sony laptop screen it looked kinda flat. But I didn''t vote. I''ve been going slow, keeping in mind that every shot is someone''s favorite of 2008. This morning, I saw it on the ViewSonic monitor at home, the screen I do my own editing on.  I saw the bird!  Right after that, it hit me.  This is one of those rare photographs that is remarkable not for technical excellence or compositional brilliance or documentary professionalism (even thought it has all of that) but for its impact.  I''m voting it a 10 because of the afterimage it created in my memory, the thoughts it inspired me to think. Thank you!</td>', 'First saw this on the Dell monitor at work & thought "snapshot."  On the Sony laptop screen it looked kinda flat. But I didn''t vote. I''ve been going slow, keeping in mind that every shot is someone''s favorite of 2008. This morning, I saw it on the ViewSonic monitor at home, the screen I do my own editing on.  I saw the bird!  Right after that, it hit me.  This is one of those rare photographs that is remarkable not for technical excellence or compositional brilliance or documentary professionalism (even thought it has all of that) but for its impact.  I''m voting it a 10 because of the afterimage it created in my memory, the thoughts it inspired me to think. Thank you!', '2009-01-19 14:16:12.000000', NULL, 1),
