(5211781, 756078, 83313, '<td valign="top">A pleasing scene. You should have used the entire 720 pixels allowed in at least one direction, however.<br/> <br/>Also, your file size of only 47k indicates a highly compressed image and that may be robbing a lot of additional detail and sharpness from this image. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (200k for this one)</td>', 'A pleasing scene. You should have used the entire 720 pixels allowed in at least one direction, however. Also, your file size of only 47k indicates a highly compressed image and that may be robbing a lot of additional detail and sharpness from this image. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (200k for this one)', '2009-01-22 13:35:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5211782, 756348, 86447, '<td valign="top">I don''t like the crop cutting his eye in half.   If this was all you had to work with, I think it could have been cropped right down the center of his face to make an artsy statement.   As it is, it appears that an accident happened and you didn''t get all of his face in the frame.   To me, anyway...</td>', 'I don''t like the crop cutting his eye in half.   If this was all you had to work with, I think it could have been cropped right down the center of his face to make an artsy statement.   As it is, it appears that an accident happened and you didn''t get all of his face in the frame.   To me, anyway...', '2009-01-22 13:36:02.000000', NULL, 1),
