(5211869, 756293, 61234, '<td valign="top">Another great shot from Iceland. No wonder this is one of the happiest place on earth (as per the book I''m currently reading, The Geography of Bliss).<br/>It looks very much like its namesake. Well done!</td>', 'Another great shot from Iceland. No wonder this is one of the happiest place on earth (as per the book I''m currently reading, The Geography of Bliss).It looks very much like its namesake. Well done!', '2009-01-22 14:14:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5211880, 755999, 60495, '<td valign="top">Not real keen on this one and heres why, the image looks to bright and the smoke is blown out which removes all the detail, smoke shots are tough to do and lighting and exposure are key to making them look right. IMO I would also have cropped the image so the main section of smoke was further to the right which would have helped balance the image. Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Not real keen on this one and heres why, the image looks to bright and the smoke is blown out which removes all the detail, smoke shots are tough to do and lighting and exposure are key to making them look right. IMO I would also have cropped the image so the main section of smoke was further to the right which would have helped balance the image. Good luck in the challenge.', '2009-01-22 14:19:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5211884, 756698, 60495, '<td valign="top">I only scored this one a 4 and here is my reasoning, hope the information helps.<br/> <br/>The bird tends to get blend into the background, with this being an advanced rule set there are ways the background could have been toned down to bring more focus to the bird. If you have PS you can make layers of only the background or only the bird then make adjustments to help make the bird a focal point rather than just part of the image. Also cropping the right side to put the bird at the 1/3 line and cropping tighter on the bird would help. Alway think about what does not help the image hurts the image.</td>', 'I only scored this one a 4 and here is my reasoning, hope the information helps. The bird tends to get blend into the background, with this being an advanced rule set there are ways the background could have been toned down to bring more focus to the bird. If you have PS you can make layers of only the background or only the bird then make adjustments to help make the bird a focal point rather than just part of the image. Also cropping the right side to put the bird at the 1/3 line and cropping tighter on the bird would help. Alway think about what does not help the image hurts the image.', '2009-01-22 14:20:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5211886, 755598, 68546, '<td valign="top">Lovely picture but waaay too much work done on the eyes. Everything else is great it''s just the overly white eyes really detract from the lovely soft shot.</td>', 'Lovely picture but waaay too much work done on the eyes. Everything else is great it''s just the overly white eyes really detract from the lovely soft shot.', '2009-01-22 14:22:07.000000', NULL, 1),
