(5213436, 755125, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oh, Anni, I loved this photo!   What a moment you captured.   Just last week walking around downtown I took pictures of a window washer going for a "look" like this.  But mine was boring and bleh.  This is GREAT!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh, Anni, I loved this photo!   What a moment you captured.   Just last week walking around downtown I took pictures of a window washer going for a "look" like this.  But mine was boring and bleh.  This is GREAT! ', '2009-01-23 00:07:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5213438, 754507, 88136, '<td valign="top"><b>Commments from my first edit of this image</b>.<br/> <br/>redjulep<br/> Canon EOS-350D Rebel XT  12/12/2008 11:52:34 AM  This is an outstanding image. Yes, a highly personal moment, but it serves to help us all remember. Thanks for posting it. <br/> <br/> <br/>patio127<br/> Canon EOS-40D  12/12/2008 09:36:52 AM  <br/>well done-we need to remember.... <br/> <br/> <br/>MaryO<br/> Nikon D200  12/12/2008 08:54:37 AM  <br/>This brings back the first time I saw this memorial in person. If you know anything at all about the conflict and the memorial you just can''t help being drawn into the sadness of all those deaths as the names on the wall just keep coming. My father was the navigator on missions bringing some of those kids back to the States for burial ... hell of a job. <br/> <br/> <br/>iamwoman<br/> Canon EOS-30D  12/12/2008 04:22:10 AM  <br/>It''s a great moment well captured. <br/> <br/>You took this because that what we do - we record life. <br/> <br/>I''m sure you were respectful. <br/> <br/> <br/>Melethia<br/> Canon EOS-30D  12/12/2008 04:01:00 AM  <br/>This is an excellent image. I understand your hesitation, both with taking the picture and sharing it, but I''m glad you did both. I find the reflection of the young man at the edge of the frame really adds to this - he cannot know the depth of the emotion of the man touching the wall, but perhaps it will cause him to pause for a second and think. <br/> <br/> <br/>nixter<br/> Canon EOS-350D Rebel XT  12/12/2008 03:25:44 AM  <br/>wow full of emotion! A strong photo journalistic shot! <br/>I''m curious to know what he''s listening to... <br/> <br/> <br/>MattO<br/> Canon EOS-1D Mark III  12/12/2008 12:42:33 AM  <br/>This is a very strong emotional image. I like this shot quite a bit, the reflection is very nice and the composition is nice. <br/> <br/> <br/>Ken<br/> Canon EOS-40D  12/12/2008 12:04:36 AM  <br/>Wow. This leaves me speechless.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-01-23 00:11:43.</i></td>', 'Commments from my first edit of this image. redjulep Canon EOS-350D Rebel XT  12/12/2008 11:52:34 AM  This is an outstanding image. Yes, a highly personal moment, but it serves to help us all remember. Thanks for posting it.   patio127 Canon EOS-40D  12/12/2008 09:36:52 AM  well done-we need to remember....   MaryO Nikon D200  12/12/2008 08:54:37 AM  This brings back the first time I saw this memorial in person. If you know anything at all about the conflict and the memorial you just can''t help being drawn into the sadness of all those deaths as the names on the wall just keep coming. My father was the navigator on missions bringing some of those kids back to the States for burial ... hell of a job.   iamwoman Canon EOS-30D  12/12/2008 04:22:10 AM  It''s a great moment well captured.  You took this because that what we do - we record life.  I''m sure you were respectful.   Melethia Canon EOS-30D  12/12/2008 04:01:00 AM  This is an excellent image. I understand your hesitation, both with taking the picture and sharing it, but I''m glad you did both. I find the reflection of the young man at the edge of the frame really adds to this - he cannot know the depth of the emotion of the man touching the wall, but perhaps it will cause him to pause for a second and think.   nixter Canon EOS-350D Rebel XT  12/12/2008 03:25:44 AM  wow full of emotion! A strong photo journalistic shot! I''m curious to know what he''s listening to...   MattO Canon EOS-1D Mark III  12/12/2008 12:42:33 AM  This is a very strong emotional image. I like this shot quite a bit, the reflection is very nice and the composition is nice.   Ken Canon EOS-40D  12/12/2008 12:04:36 AM  Wow. This leaves me speechless.', '2009-01-23 00:07:54.000000', '2009-01-23 00:11:43.000000', 0),
