(5215011, 756314, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  As you know, I think this is an excellent series of images.  I just looked and noted the differences between:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=655783" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/40000-44999/41746/120/655783.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/40000-44999/41746/120/655783.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/40000-44999/41746/120/655783.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Tones aside (I like the color too), I think I like her glance in the b&amp;w, just seems to capture her character a little more.. if that makes sense.</td>', 'I gave this an 8.  As you know, I think this is an excellent series of images.  I just looked and noted the differences between:   Tones aside (I like the color too), I think I like her glance in the b&w, just seems to capture her character a little more.. if that makes sense.', '2009-01-23 17:39:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5215021, 756700, 83080, '<td valign="top">I love the way you captured this.  When you started off the ''08 March Macro challenge with <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=653207" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this other velvet staghorn shot</a> &amp; followed it up with your Best of ''08 entry above, it was like you were throwing down the gauntlets &amp; challenging/inspiring the rest of us to take some interesting photos.  I have to admit, your day 1 velvet staghorn shot is my personal favorite, but I do love this one too.</td>', 'I love the way you captured this.  When you started off the ''08 March Macro challenge with this other velvet staghorn shot & followed it up with your Best of ''08 entry above, it was like you were throwing down the gauntlets & challenging/inspiring the rest of us to take some interesting photos.  I have to admit, your day 1 velvet staghorn shot is my personal favorite, but I do love this one too.', '2009-01-23 17:42:55.000000', NULL, 0),
